<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turnout at Israel's election has reached a record high at the halfway stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0e8ce2321cbbe273b88f281b9a797d436a8c110b86ec92f171d4e9552556d6d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turnout-at-israel-s-election-has-reached-a-record-high-at-the-halfway-stage/live-79713839--49f6cc43b4e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turnout-at-israel-s-election-has-reached-a-record-high-at-the-halfway-stage/live-79713839?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Almost 45% of the electorate had voted by 2 p.m., the highest share since such records began in 1973. The highly anticipated vote is expected to be a close-fought contest, and perhaps even a stalemate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd88968447adafde6b8e27a7b44ccae39a59d5d5bdd29a901d782116fc102cba</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark's Frederiksen criticizes Finland and Norway for calling Putin without coordinating with allies, despite consultation with Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93694549088f239b91a9a1d5c47fb44aeeeec06441a88e5fac188a7de69d1006</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/denmark-s-frederiksen-criticizes-finland-and-norway-for-calling-putin-without-coordinating-with-alli/a-79776208--b9062a9ff501.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/denmark-s-frederiksen-criticizes-finland-and-norway-for-calling-putin-without-coordinating-with-allies-despite-consultation-with-ukraine/a-79776208?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland and Norway have called Putin about ending the Ukraine war, drawing Danish criticism. The dispute highlights divisions over European engagement with Moscow ahead of planned US-led peace talks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan acknowledges civilian casualties in Syria airstrike against 'Islamic State'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e2261c4ef39cc21a2f60cda0d3b552ac3a98b9a09d01daed686230c1ba55386</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jordan-acknowledges-civilian-casualties-in-syria-airstrike-against-islamic-state/a-79775653--7282e0a35d06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jordan-acknowledges-civilian-casualties-in-syria-airstrike-against-islamic-state/a-79775653?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Jordanian government spokesman has expressed "regret" over civilian casualties in an airstrike it said was targeting "IS" militants.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo reports over 10,000 Ebola cases as the outbreak spreads abroad, with no approved vaccine or specific treatment for the Bundibugyo virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a86d267ccf38318b6f5c077937b13d252ec4524579263ba2bb0d91c82bb2c4c8</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-/a-79773667--055ba7810ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-specific-treatment-for-the-bundibugyo-virus/a-79773667?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DR Congo has reported more than 10,000 Ebola cases and nearly 4,900 deaths. The outbreak involves a virus for which there is no approved vaccine or specific treatment, complicating efforts to contain its spread.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz says erosion of global order means middle powers in Europe and Asia must be more assertive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:198ecafbb19a93cf6d4c2f381d4ac425573905bd1966ffc0633f0b3b13944580</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-asse/live-79772992--98272a034e7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-assertive/live-79772992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Singapore, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Europe and Germany want to increase free trade with open competition, reliability and a rules-based order.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two men face UK national security charges following an incident near RAF Fairford, with police suspecting Iranian state involvement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d1a363eee8400e326663bcd2637f72fd211cdd8474173fcbbd9915731e3c73</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-men-face-uk-national-security-charges-following-an-incident-near-raf-fairford-with-police-suspec/a-79773432--5ee211ad289a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-men-face-uk-national-security-charges-following-an-incident-near-raf-fairford-with-police-suspecting-iranian-state-involvement/a-79773432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">British prosecutors have charged two men over an incident near RAF Fairford in September. Police suspect Iranian involvement in the case at a base used for US strikes on Iran.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police in northern Germany search for suspects after car ramming overnight injures several</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfdb620eb311e0fcb7e23eba5d0c28859e4c7c0fe72202715b16453e2c07753d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-in-northern-germany-search-for-suspects-after-car-ramming-overnight-injures-several/a-78107062--249602b37b60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-in-northern-germany-search-for-suspects-after-car-ramming-overnight-injures-several/a-78107062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A person intentionally drove into a group of people in a northern German town, police have said. Three people have been taken into custody in what police said was likely a gang confrontation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Arunachal sees fresh violence over proposed dam</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7aab5aa480c7ef853f2475877b006a9413bdca943595ea061aea31c7f6fa735</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650--d59bfea6f557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More violence erupted in India's northeastern state of Arunachal Pradesh over proposed hydroelectric projects that locals are protesting. Also, India's top court will hear pleas against the poll body chief.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil elections: Merz, world leaders congratulate Lula on his win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1244b7d41010d5da031e1a3a3ee25ccab2f2777151624485d53022ab364b1b39</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T04:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-elections-merz-world-leaders-congratulate-lula-on-his-win/live-79755630--42141a0af1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-elections-merz-world-leaders-congratulate-lula-on-his-win/live-79755630?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Lula secured a surprise win over far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, whose party recognizes Lula's election victory.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia begin Oleshky ceasefire for aid mission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:824532cec68b0dfdd01f465f20f380cbf939d6d5e253f63f4653022da6cc526d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T03:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-begin-oleshky-ceasefire-for-aid-mission/a-79771473--bf865826a254.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-begin-oleshky-ceasefire-for-aid-mission/a-79771473?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Around 2,000 people remain stranded in the city of Oleshky, facing severe shortages of food and medicine. The Russian-occupied town has been devastated by fighting and flooding since Moscow's invasion in 2022.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US seeks new charges against former FBI chief James Comey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:773572bdf2965d20989cbb38e198457ded7075fc995369ce41bc5621e49c358d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T01:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-seeks-new-charges-against-former-fbi-chief-james-comey/a-79771256--b8a272db5879.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-seeks-new-charges-against-former-fbi-chief-james-comey/a-79771256?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration accuses the former FBI director of leaking classified information a decade ago. Comey denies wrongdoing, while his lawyers argue the case is legally invalid and comes too late.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>England and Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane wins Ballon d'Or</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff21d1ab64358e5a1f8bd28e4c8eb702899a1c1a5d0bc47ba27747247a4d0f01</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067--21e06316b487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The England captain ends his country's 25-year wait for the prestigious award after scoring 73 goals for club and country last season, beating competition from Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan says its military struck 'militant hideouts' in Syria after deadly church attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7678179a94cd1680b9deb404591b3a0c8b46fe62582712815ff671f7031022fc</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T22:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jordan-says-its-military-struck-militant-hideouts-in-syria-after-deadly-church-attack/a-79760441--3812591acdd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jordan-says-its-military-struck-militant-hideouts-in-syria-after-deadly-church-attack/a-79760441?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jordanian armed forces carried out strikes on "militant hideouts" in Syria that it said were linked to a deadly church attack on the kingdom last week. Syria gave a different account.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN sounds the alarm over Israel's West Bank military operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b87fa3df9fb74bbb8f3493f054e95ef9867cd48b1868e998fd1ab7ced84b9cb</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T20:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-sounds-the-alarm-over-israel-s-west-bank-military-operation/a-79770228--2f8db957dcd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-sounds-the-alarm-over-israel-s-west-bank-military-operation/a-79770228?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN has sounded the alarm on Israeli action in the West Bank city of Hebron after hundreds of families were displaced over the weekend. Israel has ordered the military to demolish homes after soldiers were killed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A bad omen? Syria bans women from university courses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a655ddd0686375da31ae3348b7b252ca87a115dcfb85d04cd4d1bcee9904c8f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T20:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348--ba55f3eb7dc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-bad-omen-syria-bans-women-from-university-courses/a-79769348?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The recent announcement that Syrian tertiary institutes will not allow women into some courses has triggered debate. Critics worry it may be a sign that the new Syrian government is restricting women's rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AI company Anthropic files its IPO in hopes of raising $100 billion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36a71a07860b325ba257e321d05ac06f7ee663b71b53b646edcff4cee3e7da30</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T18:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-company-anthropic-files-its-ipo-in-hopes-of-raising-100-billion/a-79768876--0dae568d3f2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-company-anthropic-files-its-ipo-in-hopes-of-raising-100-billion/a-79768876?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic has filed paperwork for an initial public offering that could be one of the biggest in history. The co-founders have outlined both the benefits and the risks of AI in their pitch to potential investors.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe cruise ship captain after Bremerhaven collision</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8216eb6a15cdba2b04229d9943a2392e2a5ff6e92e15094957cd540bfe69c803</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-cruise-ship-captain-after-bremerhaven-collision/a-79769346--ffe109304bf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-cruise-ship-captain-after-bremerhaven-collision/a-79769346?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A three-ship collision has led to the cancellation of a cruise and expensive damages. Shipyard repairs are needed, and further cruises could be affected.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Germany thinks of carmaker Audi's $4 billion deal with Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f01f3b5d2a5d4453e9e19f9d05e6d1052dbabdde0c26f2b228f604d8baaa4035</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479--6c6f86b95e86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The luxury carmaker is set to open its first factory in the United States — a move Trump credits to his tariffs. DW examines the German reaction amid a massive auto industry cull at home.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine may be involved in Mali's conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed0ef7bb1497fb734146f8129c26a80baff6690efa1eb98e7d42b24a6e2d9b5</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423--7ee87f683a22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ukraine-may-be-involved-in-mali-s-conflict/a-79743423?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Allegations that Ukrainian specialists are supporting Tuareg rebels in Mali highlight Kyiv's effort to challenge Russian influence far beyond the battlefield in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
